IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 2712 of 2013
CITATION: (2013) 6 SCC 1
YEAR: 2013

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: Aftab Alam, Ranjana P. Desai

PARTIES:
Novartis AG vs Union of India

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Patents Act, 1970

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 3(d) Patents Act

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
evergreening of patents, enhanced efficacy, gleevec anticancer, public health access

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Denied patent for beta crystalline form of Imatinib Mesylate, upholding Section 3(d) as valid safeguard against evergreening of pharmaceutical patents.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 3(d) Patents Act.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

